      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nThe Anchor is an exceptional detached family residence with a detached double garage, occupying an elevated site of approximately circa 0.25 acres. The property commands uninterrupted panoramic view across Sandycove bay, Sandycove island and the Preghane point on Castlepark peninsula, enjoying one of Kinsale's most spectacular coastal setting.\n\nBeautifully presented and meticulously maintained throughout, the accommodation has been thoughtfully designed to maximise both natural light and the magnificent maritime outlook. Quality finishes include engineered oak flooring, expansive picture windows that perfectly frame the ever changing seascape, a bespoke solid cherry wood kitchen with granite worktops and centre island, and well appointed bathroom suites. Many of the principal rooms enjoy breathtaking coastal views, creating a wonderful sense of tranquility and connection with its natural scenic surrounding landscape. This home was constructed in 1982 by the highly regarded local builder Joe Neville & Sons. \n\nThe accommodation is centred around an impressive reception hall featuring a striking open tread staircase. The elegant dual aspect living room is flooded with natural light and opens directly onto a sun drenched south facing patio, an ideal setting for outdoor entertaining and relaxation. Glazed double doors lead through to the dining room, which connects seamlessly to the kitchen via a feature archway, creating an excellent flow between the principal living spaces.\n\nThe ground floor accommodation further comprises three generous double bedrooms, including a superb principal suite complete with walk-in wardrobe and luxurious en suite shower room. A well-appointed family bathroom and fully fitted utility room complete the accommodation at this level.\n\nAt first floor level there is a further spacious double bedroom, a shower room and a versatile additional room currently configured as a dressing room, offering excellent flexibility for use as a home office, study or hobby room.\n\nApproached through electronic entrance gates, visitors are immediately welcomed by a distinctive anchor mounted on a limestone plinth, setting the tone for this unique coastal home. A sweeping driveway leads to a generous parking area and detached double garage, providing ample space for vehicles, boat storage or workshop use.\n\nThe grounds have been carefully landscaped to complement the property's exceptional setting and are predominantly laid out in lawn with a variety of mature shrubs and trees. Limestone pathways extend around the perimeter of the house, leading to an attractive rear rockery garden adorned with colourful roses. The expansive south-facing patio enjoys all day sunshine and provides the perfect vantage point from which to savour the spectacular sunsets over Sandycove Island while entertaining family and friends.\n\nThe Anchors is located just a short stroll from Sandycove, a peaceful and highly sought after coastal enclave only five minutes from Kinsale. Nestled within a sheltered bay protected by Sandycove Island, the area is renowned for its safe swimming waters, sailing, kayaking and boating opportunities. The sandy shoreline and island provide a wonderful natural amenity, while the surrounding coastline offers excellent opportunities for walking, cycling and enjoying the outdoors.\n\nLocal educational facilities are well catered for, with a school bus service to the nearby village of Ballinspittle and Kinsale Community School, which enjoys an excellent reputation. The renowned Bandon Grammar School is also within easy reach and offers a boarding option.\n\nKinsale, one of Ireland's most celebrated harbour towns, is steeped in history and character, with landmarks including Charles Fort, James Fort and St Multose Church. The town is internationally renowned for its vibrant culinary scene, bustling marina, yacht clubs and colourful streetscape, all of which contribute to its reputation as one of Ireland's premier lifestyle destinations. Golf enthusiasts are particularly well served, with both Kinsale Golf Club at Farrangalway and the world-famous Old Head Golf Links within easy driving distance.\n\nCork City, Ireland's second-largest city, is approximately 35 km away and provides a wealth of commercial, educational and cultural amenities, together with an international airport, mainline rail services and major port facilities.\nDistances (approx.)\n\nKinsale Town 3.8km (6 minutes)\nCork City Centre: 31 km (37 minutes)\nCork Airport: 25 km (30 minutes)\nDublin City Centre: 279 km (3 hours 18 minutes)\nDublin Airport: 290 km (3 hours 15 minutes)\nShannon Airport: 153 km (2 hours 15 minutes)"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nReception Hall - 7.00m x 2.94m\nThis is a bright and spacious reception area featuring a striking open-tread staircase and warm engineered oak flooring. A long feature window frames attractive views towards Preghane Point on Castlepark Peninsula, filling the space with natural light and creating a wonderful sense of connection to the surrounding landscape.\n\nLiving Room - 5.25m x 4.36m\nA beautifully bright and comfortable dual-aspect reception room, featuring large picture windows and a sliding patio door opening onto a sun drenched south facing patio. From here, uninterrupted views can be enjoyed across Sandycove Bay, Sandycove Island and Preghane Point on Castlepark Peninsula. The room is further enhanced by a marble open fireplace, engineered oak flooring, elegant plaster coving and ceiling rose, together with both wall and ceiling lighting. Glazed panelled doors provide direct access to the adjoining dining room.\n\nDining Room - 4.37m 4.23m\nWith an archway providing direct access to the kitchen, this inviting dining room enjoys a large south facing window that captures delightful views towards Sandycove Island. The room is further enhanced by a marble open fireplace, engineered oak flooring, elegant plaster coving and ceiling rose, together with both wall and ceiling lighting, creating a warm and welcoming space for entertaining and family dining.\n\nKitchen - 5.72m x 2.81m\nQuality solid cherry wood kitchen fitted with an extensive range of eye and floor level units, incorporating glass display cabinets, display and under-counter lighting, together with polished granite worktops and matching splashbacks. A central island unit provides additional granite worktop space, generous storage and an integrated wine rack. A full range of kitchen appliances is included in the sale, comprising a hob, double oven, microwave, dishwasher and fridge. The floor is tiled throughout, while double doors open directly onto the attractive rear rockery garden, creating an excellent connection between the indoor and outdoor living spaces.\n\nUtility Room - 2.83m x 1.81m\nFully fitted with an excellent range of eye and floor level units, complemented by generous countertop workspace and an integrated sink unit. The room is plumbed for both a washing machine and dryer, which are included in the sale. Tiled flooring throughout ensures practicality and ease of maintenance, making this an ideal ancillary space for everyday household needs.\n\nPrinciple Bedroom - 3.88m x 3.80m\nLovely bright dual aspect principal bedroom enjoying wonderful views towards the Castlepark Peninsula, Sandycove Bay and the surrounding coastline. This spacious and comfortable bedroom is filled with natural light and features engineered oak flooring, creating a warm and relaxing environment.\n\nWalk-in Wardrobe - 2.15m x 1.66m\nFully fitted with quality walnut hanging space and built-in drawer units, providing excellent storage and organising options. The room is finished with an engineered oak floor, enhancing the warmth and quality of the space.\n\nEn-Suite - 2.95m x 1.53m\nQuality three-piece shower suite comprising a large walk-in shower cubicle with pressure rainhead shower fitting, twin his and her wash hand basins set within a built-in storage unit and granite worktop. The room is further enhanced by a tiled floor, partially tiled walls and two heated towel rails, creating a stylish and luxurious finish.\n\nBedroom 2 - 3.87m x 3.35m\nGenerous double bedroom enjoying attractive views towards the Castlepark Peninsula and Sandycove beyond. This bright and comfortable room features a wash hand basin with built-in under storage unit and is finished with an engineered oak floor.\n\nBedroom 3 - 3.87m x 3.34m\nSpacious double bedroom enjoying attractive views towards the Castlepark Peninsula and Sandycove. Bright and comfortable throughout, this well-proportioned room is finished with an engineered oak floor.\n\nMain Bathroom - 2.82m x 2.74m\nFeaturing a quality five-piece suite comprising a bath, separate shower cubicle with electric shower fitting, WC, bidet and wash hand basin with overhead vanity unit. The bathroom is finished with a tiled floor and partially tiled walls, providing a well-appointed space.\n\nFirst Floor Landing - 3.21m x 1.75m\nProviding access to all first floor rooms. There is an engineered oak floor.\n\nBedroom 4 - 3.62m x 3.13m\nBright double bedroom enjoying elevated views towards Sandycove Island and the surrounding coastline. Filled with natural light, this attractive room features an engineered oak floor and a built-in closet.\n\nShower Room - 3.20m x 1.28m\nFeaturing a quality three-piece shower suite comprising a large shower cubicle with pressure rainhead shower attachment, WC and wash hand basin. The room is finished with a tiled floor, partially tiled walls and an illuminated wall mirror.\n\nHome Office / Dressing Room - 3.12mx 2.91m\nA versatile room ideally suited for use as a home office or walk-in dressing room. The space is currently fitted with quality walnut built-in wardrobes, providing excellent storage accommodation, and is finished with an engineered oak floor. In addition, there is a separate built-in storage closet, further enhancing the practicality of the room.\n\n"
      },
